onths for the 50 states and selected cities and counties.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"National 1-dose vaccination-coverage levels among children aged 24--35 months increased from 17.6% in 2004 to 21.3% in 2005.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"incidence of acute HAV infections have declined to the lowest level ever recorded\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Data are weighted to adjust for households with multiple telephone lines, household nonresponse, and noninclusion of households without landline telephones\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"NIS conducts a random-digit--dialed telephone survey of households and a mail survey of the children's vaccination providers\"}, {\"loc\": \"ocr\", \"q\": \"Estimate not reported because it is unstable; 95% CI is >20%\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\"]}", "type": "text"}]}